    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Bug Type:</b> Visual / UI Layout / Responsive Design</p>

<p><b>Priority:</b> Medium</p>

<p><b>Preconditions:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Game is running.</li>
	<li>The player is on the Main Menu.</li>
	<li>The CONTROLS &amp; MECHANICS button is available.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Launch Keep Fighting &amp; Earning.</li>
	<li>Stay on the Main Menu.</li>
	<li>Click <b>CONTROLS &amp; MECHANICS</b>.</li>
	<li>Observe the modal's width, text layout, and Close button.</li>
	<li>Check the long control descriptions for Doraemon, Miyabi, and Lương Thơ.</li>
	<li>Observe whether the modal fits within the game window.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>The Controls &amp; Mechanics modal is centered and fully visible within the game window.</li>
	<li>All control descriptions are displayed correctly.</li>
	<li>Long text automatically wraps to the next line.</li>
	<li>The Close button remains fully visible and accessible.</li>
	<li>The modal adjusts to the available screen space without clipping its content.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>The modal extends beyond the right edge of the game window.</li>
	<li>Long control descriptions are displayed on a single line instead of wrapping.</li>
	<li>Some text is clipped and cannot be read completely.</li>
	<li>The Close button is partially outside the visible area.</li>
	<li>The modal layout does not properly fit the available screen space.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Test Case Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li><b>FAIL</b></li>
	<li><b>Testing Type:</b> Exploratory Testing</li>
	<li><b>Related Module:</b> Main Menu / Controls &amp; Mechanics</li>
	<li><b>Regression Testing:</b> Required after the UI layout is corrected.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Notes:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>The issue appears to be related to improper text wrapping and modal size constraints.</li>
	<li>Long character-specific control descriptions may cause the content container to expand beyond the intended width.</li>
	<li>Check whether the text Label has automatic wrapping enabled.</li>
	<li>Verify the layout and size constraints of the modal's containers.</li>
	<li>Consider using a ScrollContainer to accommodate long instructions.</li>
	<li>Check whether the issue occurs at multiple screen resolutions.</li>
	<li>Ensure that the Close button remains accessible after resizing the game window.</li>
	<li>Verify that all control descriptions remain readable after the fix.</li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
